# Uchbenbak, the Great Mistake (descend 8): "{3}{U}{B}... {4}{U}{B}: Return this card from your graveyard to the battlefield with a finality counter on it.
# Activate only if there are eight or more permanent cards in your graveyard and only as a sorcery." Bot1's five Thought Scours (instants,
# no permanent cards) mill Uchbenbak itself and then, over turns 1 and 3, six more permanent cards and a Lightning Bolt: seven permanent
# cards in all. On turn 5, with the whole {4}{U}{B} (and one mana more) floating, the ability is refused (CR 207.2c, 110.4a), though
# Bot2's graveyard holds a Forest discarded to its hand size, which is not Bot1's own (seven and that one would be eight). A last Scour mills a Bolt and one more
# permanent card: eight. With Ornithopter on the stack the ability is refused again (CR 602.5d); once it has resolved the six
# floating mana pay for it exactly, and Uchbenbak returns untapped with a finality counter (CR 122.1h) from the graveyard (CR 113.6m).
# Turn 7: it attacks, and one Ornithopter alone (it has two) cannot block a menace creature (CR 702.111b), vigilance leaves it untapped
# (CR 702.20b), and six damage reach Bot2.

